200 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 148 0 R
/E (The Minnesota State Housing Tax Credit \(SHTC\) program is an innovative tool to expand funding for affordable housing construction across the state. The program allows corporate and individual taxpayers to contribute money to affordable housing development projects in exchange for state tax credits. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
201 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 148 0 R
/E (The program is considered a critical and innovative tool in leveraging private capital for affordable housing in Minnesota)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
202 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 148 0 R
/E ( Program Overview)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
203 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 148 0 R
/E (The State House Tax Credit Program was created in 2023 to address Minnesota's persistent shortage of affordable housing. Administered by the Minnesota Housing Finance Agency, eligible Minnesota taxpayers may contribute between $1,000 and $2 million annually and receive a state tax credit equal to 85% of their contribution. Contributors may direct their contributions to a specific eligible housing project or allow their funds to be distributed through the General Contribution Pool. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
204 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 148 0 R
/E (While many state housing tax credit programs provide credits directly to housing developers, the Minnesota model encourages voluntary contributions from independent taxpayers to directly fund affordable housing construction. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
205 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 148 0 R
/E (The program has an annual tax credit allocation cap of $9.9 million, which has allowed approximately $11.65 million in contributions to be raised each year. The program includes a sunset provision to allow for future evaluation, which would cause the tax credit to expire after December 31, 2028.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
206 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 148 0 R
/E (Around 50 affordable housing developers have used SHTC funding, including 15 Habitat for Humanity Minnesota affiliates. For Habitat for Humanity Minnesota, analyzing SHTC data is relevant to understand how this new funding source is supporting affordable homeownership accross our state and understand how to better advocate for policy changes. This report will examine the most up-to-date SHTC data from 2023-2026 to assess the program. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
